    "text": "Est. 1828 Dictionary Definition Definition Entries Near Cite this EntryCitation Save Word To save this word, you'll need to log in. Log In (out) in/into the open phrase 1 : in or to an area or place that is not covered or enclosed We slept out in the open with nothing above us but the stars. A deer walked out into the open. food left out in the open 2 : in or into a situation in which something (such as a feeling) is no longer hidden or kept secret Her true feelings were finally out in the open. He rarely fought his political battles in the open. Let's get everything out into the open. You've been lying to me, haven't you? Browse Nearby Words outing flannel (out) in/into the open out in left field See all Nearby Words Cite this Entry Style MLA Chicago APA Merriam-Webster “(out) in/into the open.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/%28out%29%20in%2Finto%20the%20open. Accessed 26 Mar. 2026. Copy Citation Love words? Need even more definitions? Subscribe to America's largest dictionary and get thousands more definitions and advanced search—ad free! Merriam-Webster unabridged More from Merriam-Webster Top Lookups Next refresh: 20 1bruh2800-pound gorilla3Chargoggagoggmanchauggagoggchaubunagungamaugg, Lake4thornily5chargoggagoggmanchauggagoggchaubunagungamaugg6banana7lake Word of the Day zany Listen to the pronunciation of zany See Definitions and Examples » Get Word of the Day daily email! Popular in Grammar & Usage See More Are You Misusing These 10 Common Words? 5 Verbal Slip Ups and Language Mistakes Is that lie 'bald-faced' or 'bold-faced'? The Difference Between 'i.e.' and 'e.g.' Why is '-ed' sometimes pronounced at the end of a word? See More Popular in Wordplay See More 12 Words for Signs of Spring The Opposite of Déjà Vu Why do we call it a 'pipe dream'? Why do we say 'fly off the handle'? Why do we call it a 'flea market'? See More Popular See More Are You Misusing These 10 Common Words? 12 Wo